{
 "contract": "C4, C5 and C10 of docs/protocol.md: the receiver's part of the stored sign-ins (board ab-v16.97.3; agent-browser's stored sign-ins design, sections 7.3, 7.6, 7.8 and 10). The act window (C10 windows.create with the mark act), the act's rules A to E (C5, act_rules), the read of the act store's cookies (act_cookies) and the act's end (act_end). agent-browser's service builds the requests; the receiver answers them. Every value is a sample, and every cookie value is a made-up test value.",
 "setScopes": {
  "lists": {
   "md": [
    "example.com"
   ]
  },
  "scopes": {
   "my-repo": "md",
   "md-gone": null
  },
  "default": null
 },
 "scope": "my-repo",
 "features": [
  "scopes",
  "act"
 ],
 "actWindow": {
  "note": "The act window: incognito true and the mark act, with the caller's scope. The receiver checks its incognito access first (chrome.extension.isAllowedIncognitoAccess), ends a left act, refuses while another incognito tab is open, then opens the window. The act tab (31) gets the scope for the list rules, but bridge.tabScopes leaves it out, and the copy holds act:30, not tab:31.",
  "req": {
   "t": "req",
   "id": "5f3a9c01-40",
   "op": "windows.create",
   "args": [
    {
     "url": "about:blank",
     "focused": false,
     "incognito": true
    },
    "my-repo",
    "act"
   ]
  },
